# Contract checkout portability (K002, Agent K — Kishore's coding agent).
#
# Git stores the canonical contract blobs with LF endings. The verification
# script hashes those files as RAW BYTES
# (scripts/verify-contract.mjs: createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(p))),
# so a checkout that converts LF to CRLF — for example a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true — fails the manifest hash checks even though the contract
# content is byte-identical apart from the line separator.
#
# Pinning LF for exactly the hashed paths makes checkout portable across
# machines and platforms without touching contract semantics, the manifest,
# or any verifier check. Attributes are per-path and override core.autocrlf
# for these files only; no global Git configuration is changed and ordinary
# source/documentation files are deliberately left to the default handling.
#
# This is repository checkout configuration, not a contract version change.
# Mohan's three mirrored repositories (auditor-frontend, auditor-backend,
# energy-ml-service) need the same two rules, since they mirror
# scripts/verify-contract.mjs and contracts/v1/** identically.

contracts/v1/** text eol=lf
scripts/verify-contract.mjs text eol=lf
